  "version": "1.0",
  "title": "Language agent with tools and memory",
  "subtitle": "Separate tool observations, persistent state, and the final response.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "method",
      "kind": "user-description",
      "locator": "method.md",
      "text": "# Language agent with tools and memory\n\nThis is an original illustrative architecture specification for testing PaperFigure, not a reproduction or a claim of research novelty.\n\nThe task is passed to the language-model controller.\n\nThe controller issues tool calls to external tools. Tool observations return to the controller on a subsequent decision step.\n\nThe controller queries persistent memory. Retrieved context returns to the controller. Memory contents are maintained externally; this overview does not imply gradient updates or automatic memory writes.\n\nThe controller emits a final response to the user.\n"
    }
  ],
